{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And they embittered.</b> It is known that the tav is a sign for feminines in most cases, and the mem for masculines, like מועדות (2 Chronicles 8:13) and מועדים (Genesis 1:14). The practice of the sages of Spain is that the binyanim of verbs are preserved and no letter is missing from the root. But this is not so; rather, noun forms are said as they are found. For the singular of מועדות is מועד, not מועדה. Should a scholar say in his own eyes that from מקום one says מקומים, and from ממקומות one says מקומה — perhaps he will open his eyes and see: for from בכור one says בכורים, 'who strikes Egypt in their firstborn' (Psalms 136:10), and behold 'and the firstborn of your herd' (Deuteronomy 14:23). If so, the singular would be בכורה. And likewise לבנים: one does not say לבן, but rather לבנה." "And the sense of 'in mortar and in bricks': to build houses and fences, and also to plow and to reap, and to prune and to gather. And this is 'all their work in the field,' and afterward he generalized all their labor for their needs." "<b>Which they served in.</b> [It means] 'they served on account of them,' [i.e.] they served in them with rigor. And the form עבד without a bet after it denotes the labor of the servant, and likewise 'I have served you' (Genesis 30:26). And if a bet follows it, it bears two meanings: one, 'on account of,' like 'and Israel served for a wife' (Hosea 12:13); the second, 'you shall not serve it with rigor,' in the manner of 'which has not been worked' (Deuteronomy 21:3), and likewise 'which shall not be worked in' (ibid. 21:4). For it is written 'and the desolate land shall be worked' (Ezekiel 36:34), and on this pattern 'as the creditor, so the one credit is extended to' (Isaiah 24:2)."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "Reading ולא תחסר as 'and no letter is missing'; the phrase could alternatively be parsed as a separate clause, but the sense flows as translated.", 2 "The phrase ישרתו בעבור שנים is textually difficult; rendered hyper-literally as 'they served on account of them,' understanding שנים as referring back to חומר ולבנים (the two materials). The syntax is compressed and may be corrupt."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:30:54.801631810Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}